flowchart TB
  accTitle: Proposed B3 workspace runtime architecture
  accDescr: Memory, agent, tool, monitor, and planner producers emit typed candidates. A registry validates provenance and scope. A coalition builder preserves member identities and relations. An authoritative admission governor applies a bounded policy and creates a workspace snapshot. A broadcast router delivers the immutable snapshot to authorized consumers. Consumer receipts and task outcomes flow to an attribution service; a separate policy learner creates candidate future policies for shadow evaluation and guarded promotion. Consumers and models cannot commit admission or authorize external actions.
  subgraph Producers
    M[Memory producer]
    A[Agent workers]
    T[Tool adapters]
    O[Monitors]
    P[Planners]
  end
  V[Candidate registry and validator]
  C[Coalition builder]
  G[Competition and admission governor]
  W[(Cycle workspace store)]
  R[Broadcast router]
  subgraph Consumers
    RC[Reasoning and action proposal]
    MC[Monitoring]
    LC[Memory and learning]
  end
  CR[Consumer receipts]
  OA[Outcome attribution]
  PL[Policy learner]
  PG[Policy registry and rollout gate]
  M --> V
  A --> V
  T --> V
  O --> V
  P --> V
  V --> C --> G --> W --> R
  R --> RC
  R --> MC
  R --> LC
  RC --> CR
  MC --> CR
  LC --> CR
  CR --> OA
  OA --> PL --> PG --> G
